<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Two different questions, and Android 12 and up lets them have different answers.
    Each section here is independent, and a section left out is fully enabled, which is
    the trap: silence means yes.

    CLOUD: no. An archive holds health records, memories somebody marked private, and
    recordings of people who are dead and cannot be asked again. That is not material to
    hand to a third party because a system default said so. It would not work anyway:
    Google's Auto Backup is capped at 25 MB per app and calls onQuotaExceeded above it, so
    a single 45 minute interview puts an archive over the line. A backup that silently
    skips the recordings and restores a database pointing at audio that is not there is
    worse than no backup, because it looks like one.

    DEVICE TO DEVICE: yes, all of it. This is the case the feature exists for, in Google's
    own words: files too large for the cloud that transfer between devices without issue.
    It is local, phone to phone, not through anybody's server, and the person chooses it
    during setup on the new phone. An archive can be the only recording of someone's voice,
    so losing it to a new handset is the failure this app must not have.

    The speech model is the one thing left behind. It is 41 MB of downloadable Vosk that
    Settings can fetch again in a minute, and carrying it would bloat the transfer of the
    part that actually cannot be replaced.

    CROSS PLATFORM: no. There is no iOS build of Arv, so a transfer would move a family's
    recordings onto a device with nothing that can open them.

    Android 11 and below cannot separate these. There, allowBackup="false" turns off cloud
    and phone to phone together, and the 25 MB cap would have defeated the transfer anyway.
    On those devices the export zip in Settings is the only way to move an archive, and the
    privacy policy says so rather than leaving somebody to find out.
-->
<data-extraction-rules>
    <cloud-backup>
        <exclude domain="root" />
        <exclude domain="file" />
        <exclude domain="database" />
        <exclude domain="sharedpref" />
        <exclude domain="external" />
    </cloud-backup>

    <device-transfer>
        <include domain="root" path="." />
        <include domain="file" path="." />
        <include domain="database" path="." />
        <include domain="sharedpref" path="." />
        <include domain="external" path="." />
        <!-- Redownloadable. See the note above. -->
        <exclude domain="file" path="vosk" />
    </device-transfer>

    <cross-platform-transfer platform="ios">
        <exclude domain="root" />
        <exclude domain="file" />
        <exclude domain="database" />
        <exclude domain="sharedpref" />
        <exclude domain="external" />
    </cross-platform-transfer>
</data-extraction-rules>
